msgstr "$[1/4,+\\infty)$"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:161
#: 5475a5c6b741417590ce961fa8f779cb
msgid "E"
msgstr "E"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:161
#: 905f79e4f2604d62b908fff0bc702b21
msgid "$[2/7,2/7]$"
msgstr "$[2/7,2/7]$"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:256
#: 212af9064d214b4da8303e1e9c82bdfa
msgid ""
"E's observed plan $(4,4.5)$ is first compared with the input-oriented VRS "
"target $(3.5,4.5)$. The decreasing-returns diagnosis therefore belongs to "
"that target, not to an unqualified point called “E.” A management report "
"should name both the projection rule and the local classification."
msgstr ""
"E 的观测方案 $(4,4.5)$ 首先与投入导向 VRS 目标 $(3.5,4.5)$ "
"比较。因此，规模报酬递减的诊断属于该目标，而不是一个未经限定、名为“E”的点。管理报告应同时说明投影规则和局部分类。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:261
#: eea355545efd43aca55c8f9d8b1cbcb7
msgid ""
"For all five organizations, the production evidence supports the reported "
"intercept interval. D's positive upper endpoint is unbounded, but that does "
"**not** mean infinite physical productivity. It means that the selected plan"
" admits no finite largest normalized supporting intercept; because every "
"admissible intercept is still positive, the decreasing-returns "
"classification remains identified. This extended boundary supports an "
"economic conclusion only when the production evidence also establishes the "
"relevant recession behavior. Without that evidence, neither the interval nor"
" the classification is justified by a numerical finding of unboundedness "
"alone."
msgstr ""
"对全部五个组织，生产证据都支持表中报告的截距区间。D "
"的正上端点无界，但这**不**表示物理生产率无穷大；它表示所选方案不存在有限的最大归一化支持截距。由于每个可接受截距仍然为正，规模报酬递减分类依然可以识别。只有当生产证据同时确立相关的技术衰退性质时，这一扩展边界才能支持经济结论。若没有这种证据，单凭数值无界这一发现，既不能证明该区间，也不能证明相应分类。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:271
#: 3cf2d0f9ff6941f388cf42ff7c1c81c2
msgid "Why an RTS category is not a response magnitude"
msgstr "为何规模报酬类别不是反应幅度"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:273
#: 2158a19068294976a60ff0425d317fa8
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"“Increasing,” “constant,” and “decreasing” summarize the direction of a "
"local scale response; they do not say how large that response is. Two "
"hospitals can both face decreasing returns while one loses very little "
"productivity as it expands and the other loses a great deal. If that "
"difference matters to a planning decision, the analyst can estimate a local "
"scale elasticity: the percentage change in the largest attainable service "
"bundle associated with a one-percent proportional change in resources "
"{cite:p}`forsund2004scale,podinovski2017rts`."
msgstr ""
"“递增”“不变”和“递减”概括局部规模反应的方向，却不说明反应有多大。两家医院可能都面临规模报酬递减，但一家在扩张时只损失很少生产率，另一家则损失很多。如果这种差异对规划决策很重要，分析者可以估计局部规模弹性：在资源按比例变化"
" 1% 时，最大可实现服务组合变化的百分比 {cite:p}`forsund2004scale,podinovski2017rts`。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:282
#: bde7a55afcf44c9d8d0be9d8abba816b
msgid "At the selected efficient target $(\\widehat x_o,\\widehat y_o)$, let"
msgstr "在所选有效目标 $(\\widehat x_o,\\widehat y_o)$ 处，令"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:284
#: 362d6807bf4d4a9191a6a9ec685b8e68
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\bar\\beta_o(\\alpha)\n"
"=\\max\\{\\beta:(\\alpha \\widehat x_o,\\beta \\widehat y_o)\\in\\mathcal "
"T\\},\n"
"\\qquad \\bar\\beta_o(1)=1.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\bar\\beta_o(\\alpha)\n"
"=\\max\\{\\beta:(\\alpha \\widehat x_o,\\beta \\widehat y_o)\\in\\mathcal "
"T\\},\n"
"\\qquad \\bar\\beta_o(1)=1.\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:290
#: 3506239e429848a2a90122ed26b38129
msgid ""
"$\\alpha$ describes a common proportional change in the represented "
"resources, while $\\bar\\beta_o(\\alpha)$ records the largest supported "
"proportional service bundle at that resource scale. The scale-up and scale-"
"down responses are the two one-sided derivatives"
msgstr ""
"$\\alpha$ 表示代表性资源的共同同比例变化，$\\bar\\beta_o(\\alpha)$ "
"记录该资源规模下证据能够支持的最大比例服务组合。扩大规模和缩小规模的反应分别由两个单侧导数给出："

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:295
#: ac34256836f24513859748e61a910037
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\epsilon_o^+=\\bar\\beta'_{o,+}(1),\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\epsilon_o^-=\\bar\\beta'_{o,-}(1),\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\epsilon_o^+\\leq\\epsilon_o^-.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\epsilon_o^+=\\bar\\beta'_{o,+}(1),\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\epsilon_o^-=\\bar\\beta'_{o,-}(1),\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\epsilon_o^+\\leq\\epsilon_o^-.\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:303
#: 716167cb345748d0b7378a8df053d839
msgid ""
"An expansion response of $0.8$, for example, says that a one-percent "
"increase in all represented resources supports approximately $0.8$ percent "
"more of the same proportional service bundle near that target. It is not an "
"estimate of revenue, profit, demand, or the productivity of an additional "
"employee considered alone."
msgstr ""
"例如，扩张反应为 $0.8$，表示在该目标附近，所有代表性资源增加 1% 可以支持同一比例服务组合增加约 "
"$0.8$%。它不是收益、利润或需求的估计，也不是单独增加一名员工的生产率估计。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:308
#: ee423687e37a42808d3fcc4792824f37
msgid ""
"DEA frontiers are piecewise linear, so scale-up and scale-down may have "
"different one-sided responses at the same efficient target. A constant-"
"returns classification can therefore be supported even when neither response"
" equals exactly one: one side of the target may be below proportional and "
"the other above proportional. This is why an RTS label should not be "
"converted into an assumed percentage effect."
msgstr ""
"DEA 前沿是分段线性的，因此在同一个有效目标上，扩大规模与缩小规模可能具有不同的单侧反应。即使两个反应都不恰好等于 "
"1，证据仍可能支持规模报酬不变：目标一侧的反应可以低于同比例，另一侧则高于同比例。因此，不能把规模报酬标签直接换算成臆定的百分比效应。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:315
#: ac3e4054c51342dbadb72f39dabfa529
msgid "The relationship between the qualitative and quantitative accounts is"
msgstr "定性账户与定量账户的关系为"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:317
#: 10ce2dae15ec408ead5b48c7fe5314d2
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\text{increasing returns:}&\\quad 1<\\epsilon_o^+\\leq\\epsilon_o^-,\\\\\n"
"\\text{decreasing returns:}&\\quad \\epsilon_o^+\\leq\\epsilon_o^-<1,\\\\\n"
"\\text{constant returns supported:}&\\quad\n"
"\\epsilon_o^+\\leq1\\leq\\epsilon_o^-.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\text{规模报酬递增：}&\\quad 1<\\epsilon_o^+\\leq\\epsilon_o^-,\\\\\n"
"\\text{规模报酬递减：}&\\quad \\epsilon_o^+\\leq\\epsilon_o^-<1,\\\\\n"
"\\text{支持规模报酬不变：}&\\quad\n"
"\\epsilon_o^+\\leq1\\leq\\epsilon_o^-.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:326
#: 8c36f070dd4c43eebf06201f54296968
msgid ""
"The last line is especially important at a kink: *constant supported* need "
"not mean one unique elasticity equal to one. It means that zero belongs to "
"the admissible support interval, so a constant-returns supporting account is"
" consistent with the target even when the two one-sided responses differ."
msgstr ""
"最后一行在折点处尤其重要：*支持规模报酬不变*并不必然意味着存在唯一且等于 1 "
"的弹性。它表示零属于可接受支持区间，因此即使两个单侧反应不同，规模报酬不变的支持账户仍与该目标相符。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:331
#: 452e54f0e0c04d4eb46c324af0a61f49
msgid ""
"Scale elasticity remains a local technical sensitivity. It is not a demand "
"forecast, a financial return, or evidence that management should change "
"size. DEAPack's `scale_elasticity` transforms the same selected target and "
"complete support interval used by `local_returns_to_scale`; it does not "
"invent a second target to obtain a more convenient response. The package "
"documentation provides the orientation-specific transformations and boundary"
" conventions. A core management report can usually stop after stating scale "
"efficiency, the projected target, and its supported RTS classification; the "
"two elasticities belong in the report when the magnitude or the asymmetry of"
" a local response matters."
msgstr ""
"规模弹性仍是一项局部技术敏感性，不是需求预测、财务回报或管理层应当改变规模的证据。DEAPack 的 `scale_elasticity` 使用 "
"`local_returns_to_scale` 所采用的同一所选目标与完整支持区间作变换，并不会为了得到更方便的反应而另造一个目标。包 "
"Documentation "
"给出了各导向的具体变换和边界约定。核心管理报告通常可以在说明规模效率、投影目标及其受支持的规模报酬分类后结束；只有当局部反应的幅度或不对称性对决策重要时，才需要报告两个弹性。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:341
#: 99eba10dde644ea9b7590e4de53274a7
msgid "What a scale result can support"
msgstr "规模结果能够支持什么"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:343
#: 4a3517c1398a474692ab1d96f811d9a4
msgid ""
"These scale assessments describe represented production opportunities. "
"Expansion or contraction decisions additionally require demand, prices and "
"costs, quasi-fixed resources, service obligations, risk, transition "
"capacity, and implementation constraints. A local response is not a "
"forecast, and a scale gap is not a business case."
msgstr "这些规模评价描述的是所表示的生产机会。作出扩张或收缩决策还需要考虑需求、价格与成本、准固定资源、服务义务、风险、转型能力和实施约束。局部反应不是预测，规模差距也不是商业论证。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:349
#: 62f88af08b9a40c695433835c0265439
msgid ""
"Most productive scale size, congestion, and short-run physical capacity ask "
"additional questions and require additional maintained quantities. In "
"particular, congestion asks whether reducing a particular excessive input "
"can raise attainable output. That claim requires a different production or "
"disposability account: decreasing returns merely describes a weaker "
"proportional response to expansion, while an ordinary input slack shows only"
" that a resource can fall without reducing output. Neither one, and neither "
"the CRS--VRS scale ratio, establishes congestion. Any analysis of these "
"concepts must state its production assumptions and evidence separately "
"rather than turn a scale-efficiency result into a broader management claim."
msgstr ""
"最优生产规模、拥挤和短期物理生产能力回答的是额外问题，也需要额外的既定数量。尤其是，拥挤考察减少某项过量投入能否提高可实现产出。这一主张需要不同的生产账户或可处置性账户：规模报酬递减只描述扩张时较弱的比例反应，通常的投入松弛量则只说明某项资源可以在不减少产出的情况下下降。二者都不能确立拥挤，CRS"
"--VRS 规模比率也不能。对这些概念的任何分析都必须分别说明生产假设与证据，不能把规模效率结果扩张成更宽泛的管理主张。"

#: ../../chapters/02-classical/scale-performance-management.md:360
#: f9631bb832be4bbbb58b4584106cefe9
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The next chapter changes the focus from common proportional gaps and local "
"scale response to variable-specific resource excesses and service "
"shortfalls: {doc}`04-sbm`."
msgstr "下一章把重点从共同比例缺口和局部规模反应转向逐项资源冗余与服务不足：{doc}`04-sbm`。"
